\\\":2060,\\\"kind\\\":\\\"code_observation\\\"},\n {\\\"id\\\":\\\"raft_commit_recalc\\\",\\\"file\\\":\\\"commitment.go\\\",\\\"start_line\\\":78,\\\"end_line\\\":104,\\\"kind\\\":\\\"code_observation\\\"}\n]\nd['experiment']={\\\"investigation_id\\\":\\\"9eb7105d2f8e48dfa54fcc262ad69cd9-question-0\\\",\n \\\"harness_path\\\":\\\"assurance_generated_test.go\\\",\n \\\"previous_id\\\":\\\"b9583729c15a4093ae9a72a4088d2cac-experiment\\\",\n \\\"revision_reason\\\":\\\"The probe now measures survival of each side's acknowledged entry: the event reports whether the isolated node's own log still contains its entry and whether the majority-side leader's log still contains its own, each alongside whether that node's FSM applied it, giving an applied-without-log operand on both sides. Scenario, isolation, waits and the two-sided apply are unchanged.\\\",\n \\\"source_ids\\\":[\\\"api_restore_committed_body\\\",\\\"api_addvoter\\\",\\\"api_apply_contract\\\",\\\"raft_quorum_size\\\",\\\"raft_electself_vote_count\\\"],\n \\\"scope\\\":{\\\"description\\\":\\\"Five-voter cluster whose leading node is restarted with RestoreCommittedLogs after a snapshot predating the membership change, isolated with one committed voter immediately after the restart. After both sides acknowledge a client write, the partition heals and the event reports, per side, whether the log store still holds that side's acknowledged entry, whether the FSM applied it, and the derived applied-without-log operand. Run with the flag on and off.\\\",\n  \\\"assumptions\\\":[\\\"A successful Apply is an acknowledgement to the client.\\\",\\\"A truncated log suffix with a retained FSM application is the divergence signature being looked for.\\\",\\\"Two seconds of healed time is a fair minimum for the two sides to exchange AppendEntries.\\\"],\n  \\\"excluded\\\":[\\\"Whole-package or repository test suites.\\\",\\\"Any claim that the entries are never lost; only this schedule and window are observed.\\\",\\\"Entry contents at the conflict index, which the probe reports as empty.\\\"],\n  \\\"parameters\\\":{\\\"voters_before\\\":3,\\\"voters_after\\\":5,\\\"isolation\\\":\\\"immediately after restart\\\",\\\"heal_settle_seconds\\\":2,\\\"apply_timeout_seconds\\\":2}},\n \\\"prefix\\\":\\\"The harness reuses the multi-voter scenario construction and the two-sided apply, then scans each side's log store between FirstIndex and LastIndex for the entry that side acknowledged and searches that side's applied slice for the same bytes, emitting minority_log_has_entry, minority_fsm_has_entry, applied_without_log, majority_log_has_entry, majority_fsm_has_entry and majority_applied_without_log together with the leadership, acknowledgement and divergence flags. No production logic is modified.\\\",\n \\\"responsibility\\\":\\\"The library owns the durability of an acknowledged entry: if a replica applies an entry that its log no longer holds, the replicas' states diverge and the acknowledgement was not durable.\\\",\n \\\"prerequisites\\\":[\n  {\\\"alias\\\":\\\"div_on\\\",\\\"event\\\":\\\"startup_before_restart\\\",\\\"conditions\\\":[{\\\"field\\\":\\\"mode\\\",\\\"op\\\":\\\"eq\\\",\\\"value\\\":\\\"div_on\\\"},{\\\"field\\\":\\\"snapshots\\\",\\\"op\\\":\\\"eq\\\",\\\"value\\\":1},{\\\"field\\\":\\\"expected_servers\\\",\\\"op\\\":\\\"eq\\\",\\\"value\\\":5}]},\n  {\\\"alias\\\":\\\"div_off\\\",\\\"event\\\":\\\"startup_before_restart\\\",\\\"conditions\\\":[{\\\"field\\\":\\\"mode\\\",\\\"op\\\":\\\"eq\\\",\\\"value\\\":\\\"div_off\\\"},{\\\"field\\\":\\\"snapshots\\\",\\\"op\\\":\\\"eq\\\",\\\"value\\\":1},{\\\"field\\\":\\\"expected_servers\\\",\\\"op\\\":\\\"eq\\\",\\\"value\\\":5}]}],\n \\\"comparisons\\\":[\n  {\\\"event\\\":\\\"mvdiv_after_heal\\\",\\\"identity_fields\\\":[\\\"mode\\\"],\\\"admission_alias\\\":\\\"div_on\\\",\n   \\\"assertion\\\":{\\\"field\\\":\\\"majority_applied_without_log\\\",\\\"op\\\":\\\"eq\\\",\\\"value\\\":False},\n   \\\"applicability_conditions\\\":[{\\\"field\\\":\\\"restore_committed_logs\\\",\\\"op\\\":\\\"eq\\\",\\\"value\\\":True},{\\\"field\\\":\\\"snapshots\\\",\\\"op\\\":\\\"eq\\\",\\\"value\\\":1}],\n   \\\"description\\\":\\\"The majority-side leader must not end up having applied an entry its own log no longer holds; the defect prediction is that it has.\\\"},\n  {\\\"event\\\":\\\"mvdiv_after_heal\\\",\\\"identity_fields\\\":[\\\"mode\\\"],\\\"admission_alias\\\":\\\"div_on\\\",\n   \\\"assertion\\\":{\\\"field\\\":\\\"applied_without_log\\\",\\\"op\\\":\\\"eq\\\",\\\"value\\\":False},\n   \\\"applicability_conditions\\\":[{\\\"field\\\":\\\"restore_committed_logs\\\",\\\"op\\\":\\\"eq\\\",\\\"value\\\":True},{\\\"field\\\":\\\"snapshots\\\",\\\"op\\\":\\\"eq\\\",\\\"value\\\":1}],\n   \\\"description\\\":\\\"The isolated node must not end up having applied an entry its own log no longer holds; the defect prediction is that it has.\\\"},\n  {\\\"event\\\":\\\"mvdiv_after_heal\\\",\\\"identity_fields\\\":[\\\"mode\\\"],\\\"admission_alias\\\":\\\"div_off\\\",\n   \\\"assertion\\\":{\\\"field\\\":\\\"minority_log_has_entry\\\",\\\"op\\\":\\\"eq\\\",\\\"value\\\":False},\n   \\\"applicability_conditions\\\":[{\\\"field\\\":\\\"restore_committed_logs\\\",\\\"op\\\":\\\"eq\\\",\\\"value\\\":False},{\\\"field\\\":\\\"snapshots\\\",\\\"op\\\":\\\"eq\\\",\\\"value\\\":1}],\n   \\\"description\\\":\\\"Control: with the committed configuration rebuilt the isolated side never acknowledges an entry, so its log cannot hold one.\\\"}]}\nit=d['interpretations'][0]\nit['rationale']=it['rationale'].replace(\\\"Not witnessed: any FSM divergence or lost acknowledged entry, because the applied-slice comparison at the conflict index did not line up and no entry was recovered after healing.\\\",\\\"A fifth check has been added and is under test for a bounded negative: after the heal, each side's own log is scanned for the entry that side acknowledged and compared with what its FSM applied; native runs show both entries still present in their own logs with applied_without_log false on both sides, so no lost entry or applied-without-log divergence was produced in this schedule, and the mechanism that would truncate a losing suffix is not excluded.\\\")\nit['limitations']=[\\\"Every observation is bounded (three second majority-leader wait, five second election window, two second apply timeout, two second heal settle), so no occurrence-rate or absence bound is established.\\\",\\\"No entry-level divergence or lost acknowledged entry is witnessed in any execution; the new bounded check reports the entries surviving in their own logs and is not a durability proof.\\\",\\\"The scenario restarts the former leader of a cluster grown by adding voters; other roles, change types, chain orders and durable stores are not explored.\\\"]\njson.dump(d,open(p,'w'),indent=2)\nprint('ok')\nPYEOF\n/home/nitro/Desktop/consensus-assurance/.venv/bin/python -I -B -c \\\"import sys; sys.path.insert(0, '/home/nitro/Desktop/consensus-assurance/src'); from consensus_assurance.cli import main; raise SystemExit(main())\\\" validate --run /home/nitro/Desktop/consensus-assurance/runs/2026-10-13_20-21-32-hashicorp_raft-real-run --submission update.json 2>&1 | tail -3\"","aggregated_output":"ok\n{\"valid\": true, \"run_id\": \"81876a26fa4a40c997892d2ca473cab3\", \"elapsed_seconds\": 2563.206437986002, \"diagnostics\": [], \"meaning\": \"Read-only validation of these bytes and saved state; no acceptance, execution or budget reservation\"}\n","exit_code":0,"status":"completed"}}
{"type":"item.completed","item":{"id":"item_8","type":"agent_message","text":"{\"submission\":\"update.json\",\"summary\":\"Turned the gap's divergence point into a measurable bounded check and stopped refining it. The probe now scans each side's own log store for the entry that side acknowledged and compares it with what that node's FSM applied, emitting applied_without_log for both the isolated node and the majority-side leader. Native runs show both acknowledged entries still present in their own logs two seconds after healing (minority_log_has_entry and majority_log_has_entry true, applied_without_log false on both sides), and the flag-off control shows the isolated side never had an entry at all — so no lost acknowledged entry and no applied-without-log divergence was produced in this schedule, and the mechanism that would truncate a losing suffix is not excluded. That bounded negative, with two divergence comparisons and its control, is submitted as an experiment (previous_id plus revision_reason recorded) for a retained receipt. The four established complete comparisons and the whole-question account are unchanged: conclusion violated, defect_claim asserted, with the new check noted in the rationale as under test and the limitation list updated so the divergence point is reported as unwitnessed rather than unreported.\"}"}}
